<title>AUSTRALIA: Calliope lists at 20 cent premium.</title>
<headline>Calliope lists at 20 cent premium.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-06-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Canadian-based Calliope Metals Corp began trading on the Australian Stock Exchange at A$1.15 on Friday, a 20 cent premium to the issue price.</p>
<p>Calliope, which is developing a A$316 million nickel and cobalt refinery at Gladstone on the coast of Queensland, offered 11 million shares at 95 cents each, raising A$10.45 million.</p>
<p>Its shares were trading at A$1.22 at 11.30 a.m. (0130 GMT).</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
